# Reactive Surface Snow Indentation Report - 2026-07-12

## Verdict

`PASS`

Ground footprint generation remains Blueprint + Niagara. Ultra Dynamic Sky was used only as a visual/material reference and as the source of two project-owned duplicated texture assets. Production content has no `/Game/UltraDynamicSky`, MCP, or UnrealMCP dependency.

## Production Assets

- `/Game/ReactiveSurface/Core/BP_ReactiveSurfaceControllerActor`
- `/Game/Cubeless/Reactive/BP_Piper_ReactivePrototype`
- `/Game/ReactiveSurface/Ground/NS_RS_Ground`
- `/Game/ReactiveSurface/Ground/MF_RS_SnowSurface`
- `/Game/ReactiveSurface/Ground/T_RS_Footprint_Debug_L`
- `/Game/ReactiveSurface/Ground/T_RS_Footprint_Debug_R`
- `/Game/ReactiveSurface/Ground/Textures/T_RS_Snow_Normal`
- `/Game/ReactiveSurface/Ground/Textures/T_RS_Snow_Scatter`
- `/Game/ReactiveSurface/Demo/M_RS_Demo_Snow`

## Implementation

- `NS_RS_Ground` remains the RT writer. Packed output is `R=indent depth`, `G=compaction/tread`, `B=raised rim`, `A=coverage/depth`.
- The Snow material reconstructs the footprint normal from finite Ground RT differences, combines it with project-owned snow micro-normal/scatter textures, and applies pixel-depth offset for indentation.
- Left/right footprint masks are sampled with an area-aware footprint at the current 40 m Ground window scale.
- A transient one-element Array DI was proven unreliable even though BP and Niagara getters contained every input. Ground now writes position and FootMeta to the same fixed 8-slot ring index and replays the bounded recent array for 30 Tick updates.
- Replay does not delay contact input and does not move old stamps. The Niagara HLSL max-composition makes repeated slots idempotent.

